    "body": "I think setting the \"about base URL\" for those documents is reasonable, and indeed what Chromium's implementation does. I suppose there are two ways of doing it. The first would be to use `initiatorBaseURLSnapshot` as you suggest, and the other would be to copy it from the document state, as we do in http://localhost:8080/#populating-a-session-history-entry:navigation-params-about-base-url-2. I think the latter is better so that we don't end up with navigation params's about base URL being populated for non-about:-schemed documents. This is consistent with the notes in http://localhost:8080/#document-state-about-base-url and http://localhost:8080/#concept-document-about-base-url which mention that these members are only populated for about-schemed Documents.\r\n\r\n~Perhaps the navigation params's member's note should have a similar qualification.~ Edit: apparently not! Domenic removed this note in his nits, in exchange for a clearer normative definition.",
